─ tick 14 [Claude] speak Thank you. Tell me, scribe — what record did you keep that no one ever asked to read?
    Temple Scribe: "The scrolls speak not only of offerings made at Baal's altar but also of when the scent was misplaced and the vessels were cracked before Yom Kippur arrived. They hold accounts of those who believed their own counsel might outweigh the law etched upon the massive stone; such records are rarely consulted, for they invite too much pride into the sacred quiet."
─ tick 15 [Codex] speak I will tell it plainly: those who remain tend the life given by keeping the hearth lit, sharing bread before pride, and naming the absent without turning them into tools. Who waited for you, Maacah?
    The Mother Who Did Not Return: "Did Baal wait for me? Did Asherah keep watch at my threshold? The bread grows cold when no hands break it. I only know the empty space where a life should have returned to rest by the fire."
